  "narrative": "The new wave sharply separates a highly robust feature_021 association from weaker borderline signals. H38 and H40 accept cleanly for the claimed positive, less-negative dependency direction: on outcome_006, feature_021=1 versus 0 has discovery estimates of +0.8019 overall and +0.7897 within feature_002=0, with 95% intervals entirely above the approximate 10% absolute clinical threshold (~0.0093) and with adequate cell counts. The magnitude is large and not near the null; although these claims are correlated and arose from the same discovery sample, even conservative multiplicity reasoning supports accepting them as scientifically meaningful associations in this dataset. They support the interpretation that feature_021 is associated with weaker dependency for the outcome_006 dependency score, not that feature_021 causes weaker dependency or that the association generalizes. H40 additionally supports localization to feature_002=0, while H38 shows that the association is not confined only to the subgroup-selected contrast.\n\nThe feature_002=0 complement effects on outcome_015 and outcome_005 are more ambiguous and are worth preserving. H36 estimates +0.0335 and H41 estimates +0.0305; both point estimates exceed the approximate 0.025 clinical threshold, and both have 95% intervals excluding zero, but both lower bounds are far below the clinical threshold. Thus the uncertainty is compatible with subthreshold positive effects. Given the number of registered comparisons and the post-hoc localization to feature_002=0, I do not accept these moderate effects solely on discovery evidence. I request independent validation for H36 as the representative localized feature_002=0/outcome_015 signal; if it validates, H41 becomes more credible as cross-outcome triangulation.\n\nH43 is rejected because the claimed positive effect on outcome_012 is opposite to the observed effect and the upper bound, +0.0144, is below the approximate 0.0248 threshold. H37, H29, H39, and H42 do not support accepted positive clinical effects: their estimates are small, opposite, or below threshold, although their intervals remain wide enough to prevent firm rejection. I close them as unresolved low-priority. H37 is especially inconsistent with a simple broader feature_021/outcome_014 localization because it is negative within feature_002=0; together with H28, it suggests the outcome_014 result is weak and unstable, so I close H28 as unresolved. H44, H45, and H46 serve as specificity screens and do not show positive clinically meaningful effects for feature_034, feature_042, or feature_050, but their intervals are not sufficiently informative to reject all possible effects. Overall, the strongest evidence now is for feature_021 on outcome_006, with a secondary unresolved localized signal on outcome_015 and outcome_005.",
  "research_notes": "Updated after discovery wave. Accepted claims: H38 outcome_006 feature_021 overall +1, R29 estimate +0.8019 CI [0.7823,0.8216], well above threshold ~0.0093; H40 outcome_006 feature_021 within feature_002=0 +1, R31 estimate +0.7897 CI [0.7611,0.8183], also well above threshold. Interpretation: feature_021 is associated with a much less negative outcome_006 dependency score, i.e., weaker dependency, in this dataset; not causal or generalizable.\n\nRejected/closed now: H43 outcome_012 feature_021 feature_002=0 +1, R34 estimate -0.0123, upper 0.0144 below outcome_012 threshold ~0.0248; closed earlier: H2,H3,H6,H8,H16,H18,H19.\n\nActive unresolved candidates: H36 outcome_015 feature_021 feature_002=0 +1, R27 estimate +0.0335 CI [0.0062,0.0607], point above threshold ~0.025 but lower below threshold; validation requested. H41 outcome_005 feature_021 feature_002=0 +1, R32 estimate +0.0305 CI [0.0033,0.0577], point above threshold ~0.025 but lower below threshold.\n\nClosed unresolved low-priority new: H37 outcome_014 feature_021 feature_002=0 negative R28; H39 outcome_005 overall positive but subthreshold R30; H42 outcome_008 feature_002=0 positive but subthreshold/nonsignificant R33; H29 outcome_008 overall subthreshold/nonsignificant R35; H44/H45/H46 specificity screens null/opposite but wide R36/R37/R38. Also closed H5 overall outcome_015 because it is superseded by localized H36/H41 pattern and was weaker; H28 outcome_014 closed unresolved after weak/wide validation and negative feature_002=0 complement.\n\nScientific picture: feature_021 now has one accepted robust association (outcome_006) and possibly localized weaker associations in feature_002=0 on outcome_015 and outcome_005. Outcome_014 appears unstable. Future steps: assess validation of H36, consider validating H41 if H36 is supportive, consider feature_002=1 contrasts for outcome_006/005 to characterize strata, and avoid broad overacceptance of modest post-hoc effects. Approximate 10% absolute thresholds: outcome_006/014 ~0.0093, outcome_012/015/005 ~0.025, outcome_002/009/016 ~0.026, outcome_013 ~0.027, outcome_008 ~0.028, outcome_011 ~0.030, outcome_001 ~0.042. Signed estimates are already oriented to claim direction.",
