_001", "comparator": "level_003", "contrast": "mean_difference", "eligibility": [], "subgroup": [], "direction": 1, "anticipated_direction": 0, "initial_status": "unresolved"}], "assessments": [{"claim": "H30", "status": "unresolved", "investigation": "deferred", "evidence": []}, {"claim": "H32", "status": "unresolved", "investigation": "deferred", "evidence": []}, {"claim": "H48", "status": "unresolved", "investigation": "deferred", "evidence": []}, {"claim": "H49", "status": "unresolved", "investigation": "deferred", "evidence": []}, {"claim": "H50", "status": "unresolved", "investigation": "deferred", "evidence": []}, {"claim": "H51", "status": "unresolved", "investigation": "deferred", "evidence": []}, {"claim": "H52", "status": "unresolved", "investigation": "deferred", "evidence": []}, {"claim": "H53", "status": "unresolved", "investigation": "deferred", "evidence": []}, {"claim": "H54", "status": "unresolved", "investigation": "deferred", "evidence": []}], "narrative": "No evidence assessments are due, so the main action is to refocus the next discovery wave on the one robust result so far: feature_021=1 is associated with a much less negative outcome_006 dependency score in this dataset (H38 and H40 accepted). The key scientific questions are now: (1) Is this association reproducible across important strata of accepted effect size, not merely in feature_002=0; (2) does it differ by prevalent binary features or age; (3) is it outcome-specific for outcome_006 or part of a broader dependency pattern; and (4) is it distinct from other similarly prevalent predictors. I therefore propose direct conditional mean-difference tests for feature_021 on outcome_006 within feature_034=1 and within feature_060=1, both expected positive if the accepted association is broad and robust. I also propose two interaction tests: feature_021-by-feature_034 and feature_021-by-feature_061>=55, using a positive interaction direction to test whether the less-negative association is stronger in the subgroup than in the complement; the anticipated direction is uncertain because no prior evidence strongly predicts modification. For outcome specificity, I propose a single additional overall feature_021 test on outcome_003, a low absolute threshold outcome not yet screened, rather than testing every remaining outcome; this balances breadth against multiplicity. For predictor specificity on the accepted outcome, I propose two similar-prevalence binary markers, feature_027 and feature_050, in the same less-negative direction; a null result would make feature_021 more distinctive, while a threshold-positive result would suggest a broader marker axis or correlated structure. Finally, I add a categorical screen on outcome_006 comparing feature_055 level_001 with level_003 to maintain predictor diversity. I defer several broad outcome_014/feature_005 and feature_021 outcome-panel claims that have no evidence or low prior yield, and also defer H48 because the localized feature_002=0/outcome_005 pattern was not supported by validation; this keeps the active set focused on stratum characterization, specificity, and a small number of categorical/broad screens. All proposed claims remain associations within this dataset, not causal effects or claims of generalizability. Alternative explanations include no association, opposite-direction effects, subgroup-specific heterogeneity, confounding by correlated predictors, or false-positive discovery due to multiple testing.", "research_notes": "Plan after iteration 4 explore. Accepted dataset associations: H38 outcome_006 feature_021 overall, signed estimate +0.8019 CI [0.7823,0.8216]; H40 outcome_006 feature_021 within feature_002=0, signed +0.7897 CI [0.7611,0.8183]. Interpret as weaker dependency for feature_021=1 versus 0, but only within supplied data. Rejected/closed low-prior: H2,H3,H6,H8,H16,H18,H19,H43; closed unresolved: H5,H11,H25,H26,H28,H29,H36,H37,H39,H42,H44,H45,H46. Deferred without evidence: old low-priority H15,H23,H24,H34,H35, plus newly deferred H30,H32,H48,H49-H54 to prioritize a focused wave.

Active planned wave: H27 feature_037/outcome_006 (stronger-dependency direction), H31 feature_054 level_002 vs level_001/outcome_006, H33 feature_063 level_002 vs level_001/outcome_006, H47 feature_021/outcome_006 within feature_002=1, plus new proposals: feature_021/outcome_006 within feature_034=1 and within feature_060=1; feature_021/outcome_006 interaction with feature_034=1 and with age feature_061>=55; feature_021/outcome_003 overall; feature_027/outcome_006; feature_050/outcome_006; feature_055 level_001 vs level_003/outcome_006.

Decision rules: For conditional/overall outcome_006 feature_021 estimates, accept only if signed interval clearly exceeds ~0.0093 threshold and cells adequate; interactions require unusually clear threshold separation before acceptance because they are narrower hypothesis and multiplicity-prone. For feature_027/050/55/037/categorical, do not accept unless large and interval excludes clinical threshold in proposed direction. For outcome_003, accept only if above ~0.025 threshold with precise interval; otherwise unresolved. If a new robust outcome_006 stratum or specificity marker emerges, consider one validation request; if nothing robust, prioritize alternative predictors rather than continuing broad feature_021 outcome panel. Approx thresholds: outcome_006/014 ~0.0093, outcome_005/012/015/003 ~0.025, outcome_002/009/016 ~0.026, outcome_013 ~0.027, outcome_008 ~0.028, outcome_011 ~0.030, outcome_001 ~0.042. Estimates are already signed to proposal direction."}

