  "narrative": "I assessed the eight newly delivered discovery results with the same practical 10% clinical benchmark used in this run. For these negative-centered CRISPR dependency scores, a positive returned estimate means the exposed cell is less negative than the comparator, i.e. weaker measured dependency. The relevant approximate benchmarks are 0.0093 for outcome_006 and outcome_014, and about 0.025 for outcome_005.\n\nH212 and H213 are boundary/stratification checks of the already dominant outcome_006 feature_021 signal. In the higher feature_024 stratum (>= -8), H212 gives +0.7922 [0.7644, 0.8199] with 208 versus 945 observations. In the lower feature_024 stratum (<= -8), H213 gives +0.8130 [0.7849, 0.8411] with 198 versus 649 observations. Both point estimates and lower bounds are far above the outcome_006 benchmark. Thus the feature_021=1 versus feature_021=0 association remains extremely large in both approximate log_PFS strata. I accept both as dataset-specific stability checks and close them; they reinforce H38 rather than define a new independent mechanism or population-level effect.\n\nH214 asks whether the outcome_006 feature_021 association differs between these feature_024 strata. The signed interaction estimate is -0.0208 [-0.0602, 0.0185] with cells 208 versus 945 and 198 versus 649. The point estimate is modest and opposite to the registered positive direction, but the interval crosses zero and includes clinically meaningful positive interactions because its upper bound exceeds the 0.0093 benchmark. Therefore I cannot accept evidence of effect modification, but I also cannot confidently reject a positive clinically meaningful interaction. I mark H214 unresolved and close it as an imprecise effect-modification probe. This does not weaken the main accepted feature_021-outcome_006 association; it only leaves the feature_024 boundary condition undefined.\n\nH215 and H216 are boundary probes for the narrower accepted outcome_014 feature_045 line within feature_021=1, stratified by feature_024 at -8. H215 gives +0.0939 [-0.0249, 0.2127] with 52 versus 156 observations. H216 gives +0.1230 [-0.0271, 0.2732] with 38 versus 160 observations. Both point estimates are in the clinically favorable direction and large relative to the outcome_014 benchmark, but both intervals include null and modest negative values because the cells are small. These data cannot securely establish that the feature_045-outcome_014 association persists in each approximate log_PFS stratum, though they also do not exclude a clinically meaningful positive association. I mark both unresolved and close them as boundary probes.\n\nH217 tests whether the feature_045-outcome_014 association within feature_021=1 differs between feature_024 strata. The signed interaction estimate is -0.0292 [-0.2189, 0.1605] with cells 52 versus 156 and 38 versus 160. The interval is very wide and includes both clinically meaningful negative and positive interactions. This cannot support or refute effect modification by feature_024 within feature_021=1. I mark H217 unresolved and close it.\n\nH218 extends the feature_019 level_001 versus level_002 contrast to outcome_014. The estimate is +0.0114 [-0.0274, 0.0503] with 485 versus 1132 observations. The point estimate is slightly above the outcome_014 benchmark, but the interval includes null and clinically meaningful negative and positive values. Therefore I cannot accept a clinically meaningful outcome_014 association, but I also cannot reject one because the upper bound is far above the benchmark. I mark H218 unresolved and close it. It does not materially strengthen outcome-specificity claims for the feature_045-outcome_014 line.\n\nH219 tests the same feature_019 contrast on outcome_005 with direction positive. The estimate is -0.0113 [-0.0308, 0.0082]. For the registered positive claim, the entire interval lies below the positive clinical benchmark of about 0.025, and the point estimate is negative. I therefore reject the claim of a clinically meaningful positive feature_019 level_001 versus level_002 difference for outcome_005. I note that the interval does not rule out a clinically meaningful negative association, but it does not support the claimed positive direction. This tempers any broad feature_019 generalization and supports keeping the accepted outcome_006 and outcome_014 findings outcome-specific.\n\nAs a critical reviewer, the main risk here is not cell-size validity for the outcome_006 strata, which are adequate, but multiplicity and post hoc conditioning. H212 and H213 survive multiplicity concerns because their effects are many times larger than the clinical benchmark and replicate the already accepted feature_021-outcome_006 line. H214-H217 are small-cell or interaction probes with wide intervals; they are useful as uncertainty mapping but should not be overinterpreted. If feature_024 is not baseline or is downstream of treatment, then feature_024 stratification is a descriptive conditional association and may introduce collider or temporal issues; it cannot be interpreted as causal effect modification. Predictor labels remain opaque, so biological mechanism remains unknown. Validation budget is exhausted, so I request no further validation. The accepted dataset-specific conclusions remain unchanged: a very robust positive association between feature_021=1 and weaker outcome_006 dependency, and a narrower localized positive association between feature_045=1 and weaker outcome_014 dependency within certain feature_021/feature_002 contexts, while the newer probes add precision limits rather than new independent discoveries."
